| ----- | ----- |
| **Status** | **IMPLEMENTED (2026-08-16)** |
| **Context** | Guest-auth layers lock: Marketing may become a second OTP **UI** host only after CORS on Portal public-auth + PCMS amendment. Cookie write must stay Portal BFF. `/api/me/*` must stay same-origin. |
| **Decision** | Allow credentialed CORS solely on `/api/public-auth/*`, origin-matched via GSH portal + paired marketing public origins. Add `GET /api/public-auth/session` boolean probe. Do not ship a Marketing transport adapter (Phase 5). Do not change cookie Domain helpers or `apps/api` public-auth. |
| **Consequences** | Browser on `denali.club` / `{club}.localhost` can `fetch` portal public-auth with cookies; member profile BFF stays portal-private. |
| **Dependencies** | PCMS-001 §5.4 · PCMS-CORS-01…05 · [portal-member-login-modal.mdoc](../portal-member-login-modal.mdoc) §16 Phase 4 |
| **Open questions** | None. |

### DL-46 — Marketing Portal-origin auth host (Phase 5)

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| **Status** | **IMPLEMENTED (2026-08-16)** |
| **Context** | Phase 4 CORS opened credentialed `fetch` from the paired marketing origin to Portal `/api/public-auth/*`. Marketing may now host the shared OTP/profile UI without becoming a cookie writer. |
| **Decision** | Add `tryCreatePortalOriginGuestAuthTransport` (absolute portal public-auth + `GET /api/public-auth/session`). Mount `catalogRegistrationAuthFlowSteps` in a marketing modal. PDP tour sign-in opens that modal; `[data-marketing-register]` still goes to portal register. Host `onAuthenticated` reloads the current marketing URL. Do not add Marketing BFF, CORS `/api/me/*`, or delete `/login`. **Header Sign in wiring:** see **DL-47** (navigates to Portal `/login`; not the marketing modal). |
| **Consequences** | Custom-apex guests can complete OTP without leaving marketing. `*.localhost` host-only cookies still fail-closed to guest CTAs. Portal remains the `/me/*` gate. |
| **Dependencies** | PCMS-001 §5.5 · PCMS-MKT-AUTH-01…06 · [portal-member-login-modal.mdoc](../portal-member-login-modal.mdoc) §16 Phase 5 |
| **Open questions** | None. |

### DL-47 — Marketing header Sign in stays Portal `/login` (Phase 5 surface split)

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| **Status** | **IMPLEMENTED (2026-08-16)** |
| **Context** | DL-46 shipped a working Portal-origin marketing modal. Product: guests signing in from **chrome** should land on the dedicated Portal login page; the marketing modal exists so PDP «ورود» does not leave `/tours/{id}`. A later marketing login host may reuse the same modal — header must not capture that until asked. |
| **Decision** | Header `[data-marketing-header-sign-in]` is a plain GSH `<a href={resolvePortalMemberLoginUrl}>` (Portal `/login` — presentation **DL-48** page OTP, not a portal modal). PDP `[data-marketing-tour-sign-in]` remains `MarketingLoginModalTrigger`. Keep `MarketingLoginModalProvider` in marketing layout. Auto-open `?auth=login` on marketing only for tour-detail pathnames. Do not delete Portal `/login`. Amend PCMS-MKT-AUTH-05 (1.5.1). |
| **Consequences** | Home / list / other marketing pages never open `[data-marketing-login-modal]` from the header. PDP stay-on-page OTP is unchanged. |
| **Dependencies** | PCMS-001 §5.5 · PCMS-MKT-AUTH-05 · DL-46 · [portal-member-login-modal.mdoc](../portal-member-login-modal.mdoc) §16 Phase 5 |
| **Open questions** | None. |

### DL-48 — Portal `/login` is page OTP; PDP never leaves marketing (intake Auth UI Phase 2)

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| **Status** | **IMPLEMENTED (2026-08-16)** |
| **Context** | DL-47 sends header Sign in to Portal `/login`. Live product: that page must run phone/OTP/profile **inline** (BUG-1). Auto-open `host="login"` modal blocked the page flow. Separately, API 502 showed the raw i18n key `catalogRegistration.errors.BACKEND_UNREACHABLE` (BUG-7), and PDP «ورود» fell through to portal `register?auth=login` when transport was missing / API blipped (BUG-8). |
| **Decision** | `/login` mounts `data-portal-login-full-page` + `[data-portal-login-form-panel]` + `PublicCatalogRegistrationFlow` (`memberLoginEgress`). **No** `openLoginModal` on this route. Register page stays modal-first (PCMS-UX-MODAL-04). Marketing PDP trigger `preventDefault` whenever the modal provider is mounted; missing transport still opens the dialog with translated `BACKEND_UNREACHABLE`. GSH branding fetch keeps the last **successful** snapshot on network/5xx so chrome does not flash i18n `defaultSiteName` («باشگاه») during an API blip — still never hardcode `shenski`. |
| **Consequences** | Header → page OTP. PDP stays on `/tours/{id}`. Cookie write / CORS / Layer A–E ownership unchanged. **Hygiene (PCMS 1.5.3):** `PortalLoginModalProvider` is register-only (no `host="login"` / `onLoginSessionReady`). Marketing modal context does not expose `canHostAuth`. Branding fail-soft: a later **successful** empty snapshot overwrites the previous success so a 502 cannot resurrect the old `displayName`. |
| **Dependencies** | PCMS-001 1.5.3 · DL-47 · [portal-member-login-modal.mdoc](../portal-member-login-modal.mdoc) |
| **Open questions** | None. |

### DL-49 — Guest PDP «ثبت‌نام» opens marketing modal (Phase 6)

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| **Status** | **IMPLEMENTED (2026-08-17)** |
| **Context** | DL-46/47 shipped a working PDP «ورود» modal but left `[data-marketing-register]` as a portal navigation. Product: logged-out guests who click «ثبت‌نام» on `/tours/{id}` must stay on marketing, complete phone/OTP/profile in the existing modal, then reload as a member. Header Sign in stays Portal `/login` (DL-47). Intake stays on portal after session exists. |
| **Decision** | Guest `primaryKind === "register"` uses `MarketingLoginModalTrigger` (same provider as «ورود»). Member `continue` / `view-self` / `register-another` remain portal links. No marketing BFF, no cookie write, no header modal, no auto-open on home/list. Amend PCMS-MKT-AUTH-05/06 (1.5.4). |
| **Consequences** | SMK-MKT-03 / guest funnel: modal OTP on PDP, then continue CTA → portal intake. No-JS `href` still lands on portal register. |
| **Dependencies** | PCMS-001 §5.5 · DL-46 · DL-47 · [portal-member-login-modal.mdoc](../portal-member-login-modal.mdoc) §16 Phase 6 |
| **Open questions** | None. |

